{"id":"dauernd","lemma":"dauernd","pos":"adj","rank":1661,"glosses":["constant, incessant"],"audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/90/De-dauernd.ogg/De-dauernd.ogg.mp3","examples":[{"text":"Er vergisst dauernd etwas.","en":"He is always forgetting things.","words":[{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"to forget","l":"vergessen"},null,{"g":"something"}]},{"text":"Ich fühl' mich dauernd einsam.","en":"I feel lonely all the time.","words":[{"g":"I"},{"g":"to feel","l":"fühlen"},{"g":"me","l":"ich"},null,{"g":"lonely, lone"}]},{"text":"Er beschwert sich dauernd.","en":"He is constantly complaining.","words":[{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"to weight","l":"beschweren"},{"g":"oneself"},null]},{"text":"Sie verliert dauernd ihr Taschentuch.","en":"She is always losing her handkerchief.","words":[{"g":"she / they / you"},{"g":"to lose","l":"verlieren"},null,{"g":"you (pl.) / her"},{"g":"handkerchief"}]},{"text":"Du kannst mich nicht dauernd wie ein Kind behandeln.","en":"You can't keep treating me like a kid.","words":[{"g":"you"},{"g":"can, to be able to","l":"können"},{"g":"me","l":"ich"},{"g":"not"},null,{"g":"how"},{"g":"a"},{"g":"kid"},{"g":"to treat"}]}]}